GOVERNED AI — THE TRUST ARCHITECTURE
The autopilot suggests. The captain signs.
AI MAY — ASSIST
→  Summarise, retrieve, draft handovers
→  Classify documents & prioritise tasks
→  Surface anomalies from verified records
→  Answer policy questions, role-aware
→  Forecast demand & suggest rosters
NEVER WITHOUT HUMAN SIGN-OFF
→  Prescribing or autonomous diagnosis
→  Unreviewed clinical-plan changes
→  Publishing rosters without review
→  Advice outside role or policy
→  Unrestricted tool / database access
ENFORCED BY ARCHITECTURE
→  Confidence thresholds (e.g. 0.88) route low-certainty output to humans
→  Evidence links & model provenance on every output
→  Role-based permissions & audit trails
→  Hard safety rules + override + full audit
Already production-proven: PrimeOCR’s review queue and clinician-review routing in medical triage use exactly this pattern.
